# The ledger of `x509`: what RFC 5280's certificates and lists, RFC 2986's
# requests and RFC 6125's host names let a program do, one block per
# capability, and what Rebel answers. Go 1.27's `crypto/x509` and
# `crypto/x509/pkix` are censused (`go doc -all`, 2026-11-17). Rust 1.100's
# `std` has none; the `rust` lines name the crates `rustls-pki-types` 1.15.1
# and `rustls-webpki` 0.103.16 of this machine's cargo registry (public names
# listed, their source not read). Python 3.15's standard library holds a
# little in `ssl`; the `python` lines name `cryptography.x509` of
# `cryptography` 50.0.2, installed here, which is the oracle of the tests.
# The census the author asked of other libraries, their public names listed
# on this machine on 2026-11-17: Odin's `core:crypto/x509` (`parse`,
# `verify_signature`, `verify_chain`, `verify_hostname`, `valid_at`,
# `dn_get`, `dn_string`, `serial_string`, and writers `marshal_certificate`,
# `marshal_csr`, `marshal_spki`, `marshal_pkcs8`, `marshal_dn`,
# `marshal_ext_*`), each a capability below; Zig 0.15.2's
# `std.crypto.Certificate` (`parse`, `verify`, `verifyHostName`,
# `Bundle.rescan`, `Bundle.addCertsFromFile`), the same; Java and .NET are
# not installed here (`java` finds no runtime, `dotnet` is absent), so their
# census is UNRUN. The samples were made by `cryptography` on 2026-11-17 and
# read by it and by Go: names, serials, lengths, extensions, signatures,
# chains and host names compared.

capability x509/read-der  a certificate read from its DER
  heroes  x509.decode_certificate, x509.Certificate
  go      x509.ParseCertificate, x509.Certificate
  rust    webpki::EndEntityCert, rustls_pki_types::CertificateDer
  python  x509.load_der_x509_certificate, x509.Certificate
  note    every structure read as DER; two signature algorithms that differ, an extension twice, a known extension malformed, extensions in a version below 3 are refused. A known extension's criticality written FALSE, which DER leaves out, is read (Go's and Python's answers on these four shapes UNRUN). Every byte of the sample leaf changed to 0x00, 0x80 and 0xff reads or fails, never aborts (2553 changes, tested)

capability x509/read-pem  a certificate read from PEM
  heroes  x509.parse_certificate
  go      pem.Decode then x509.ParseCertificate
  rust    rustls_pki_types::CertificateDer (its PemObject)
  python  x509.load_pem_x509_certificate, ssl.PEM_cert_to_DER_cert

capability x509/read-many  several certificates read: DER one after another, or a bundle of PEM
  heroes  x509.decode_certificates, x509.parse_certificates
  go      x509.ParseCertificates, x509.CertPool.AppendCertsFromPEM
  rust    -
  python  x509.load_pem_x509_certificates
  note    a bundle's blocks of other labels are passed over; a broken certificate fails the whole, where Go's `AppendCertsFromPEM` reports only whether any certificate was parsed (its documentation)

capability x509/write-pem  a certificate written as PEM
  heroes  x509.format_certificate
  go      pem.EncodeToMemory
  rust    -
  python  x509.Certificate.public_bytes, ssl.DER_cert_to_PEM_cert

capability x509/fields  a certificate's version, serial, validity, the bytes its issuer signed, its signature, its unique identifiers
  heroes  x509.Certificate, x509.is_valid_at
  go      x509.Certificate (Version, SerialNumber, NotBefore, NotAfter, RawTBSCertificate, Signature, Raw)
  rust    -
  python  x509.Certificate.version, x509.Certificate.serial_number, x509.Certificate.not_valid_before_utc, x509.Certificate.not_valid_after_utc, x509.Certificate.not_valid_before, x509.Certificate.not_valid_after, x509.Certificate.tbs_certificate_bytes, x509.Certificate.signature, x509.Version, x509.InvalidVersion
  note    the validity is a `time.DateTime`, so `99991231235959Z` is read and compared; an `Instant` ends in 2262. A serial of any size, past 64 bits read as Python and Go read it

capability x509/names  a distinguished name's attributes read, made, written as RFC 4514's text, an attribute's value found
  heroes  x509.Name, x509.Attribute, x509.to_name, x509.new_name, x509.format_name, x509.text_of, x509.COMMON_NAME
  go      pkix.Name, pkix.RDNSequence, pkix.RelativeDistinguishedNameSET, pkix.AttributeTypeAndValue, pkix.AttributeTypeAndValueSET, pkix.Name.FillFromRDNSequence, pkix.Name.String, pkix.RDNSequence.String
  rust    -
  python  x509.Name, x509.NameAttribute, x509.RelativeDistinguishedName, x509.Name.rfc4514_string, x509.Name.get_attributes_for_oid, x509.Name.rdns, x509.NameOID, x509.AttributeNotFound
  note    written as Python writes it, on the samples and fourteen values of its escapes: the most specific relative name first, the nine short names of RFC 4514, any other type by its dotted identifier; Go puts the attributes it knows in its own order, `CN=example.com,1.2.840.113549.1.9.1=ops@example.com` where Python and Rebel write `1.2.840.113549.1.9.1=ops@example.com,CN=example.com` (observed on the leaf). Two names are the same where their DER is; RFC 5280 § 7.1's comparison by RFC 4518's preparation is not made

capability x509/name-parse  RFC 4514's text read into a name
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  x509.Name.from_rfc4514_string

capability x509/general-names  the general names of RFC 5280 § 4.2.1.6 read
  heroes  x509.GeneralName, x509.to_general_name
  go      x509.Certificate (DNSNames, EmailAddresses, IPAddresses, URIs)
  rust    webpki::EndEntityCert::valid_dns_names, webpki::EndEntityCert::valid_uri_names
  python  x509.GeneralName, x509.GeneralNames, x509.DNSName, x509.RFC822Name, x509.UniformResourceIdentifier, x509.IPAddress, x509.DirectoryName, x509.RegisteredID, x509.OtherName, x509.UnsupportedGeneralNameType
  note    every kind read; an x400Address and an ediPartyName are kept as their DER; an iPAddress of 8 or 32 bytes is a network, its mask checked to be ones then zeros

capability x509/public-key  the subject's public key read, its kind and an RSA modulus's bits
  heroes  x509.PublicKey, x509.decode_public_key, x509.kind_of
  go      x509.ParsePKIXPublicKey, x509.PublicKeyAlgorithm, x509.PublicKeyAlgorithm.String, x509.Certificate (PublicKey, PublicKeyAlgorithm, RawSubjectPublicKeyInfo)
  rust    webpki::EndEntityCert::subject_public_key_info, rustls_pki_types::SubjectPublicKeyInfoDer
  python  x509.Certificate.public_key, x509.Certificate.public_key_algorithm_oid, x509.PublicKeyAlgorithmOID
  note    the key's kinds are `crypto/keypairs`' (RSA, P-256, P-384, Ed25519, X25519), another `unsupported`; a key a program uses is `keypairs.decode_public_der` of `der`

capability x509/signature-algorithm  a signature's algorithm and its parameters read, and the scheme that checks it
  heroes  x509.Algorithm, x509.to_algorithm, x509.scheme_of
  go      x509.SignatureAlgorithm, x509.SignatureAlgorithm.String, pkix.AlgorithmIdentifier, x509.InsecureAlgorithmError, x509.ErrUnsupportedAlgorithm
  rust    -
  python  x509.Certificate.signature_algorithm_oid, x509.Certificate.signature_hash_algorithm, x509.Certificate.signature_algorithm_parameters, x509.SignatureAlgorithmOID
  note    RSASSA-PSS's parameters read: SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512, MGF1 over the same hash, a salt as long as it, which is what `crypto/keypairs` checks; another salt is `unsupported`

capability x509/check-signature  a signature checked against a key: a certificate's against its issuer's
  heroes  x509.verify_signature, x509.is_signed_by
  go      x509.Certificate.CheckSignature, x509.Certificate.CheckSignatureFrom
  rust    webpki::EndEntityCert::verify_signature
  python  x509.Certificate.verify_directly_issued_by
  note    by `keypairs.verify_der`, the system's own cryptography, and Monocypher's for Ed25519 on macOS since 2026-11-20: RSA PKCS #1 v1.5 and PSS over SHA-2, ECDSA over P-256 and P-384, Ed25519. Ed25519 is `unsupported` on Windows, whose CNG lacks it (crypto/keypairs): the samples' Ed25519 certificate is checked on Linux, and on this Mac since 2026-11-20 (`is_signed_by`, measured that day), and where the kind is lacking the test asks `unsupported`. SHA-1 and SHA-224 are `unsupported`, as `crypto/keypairs` offers neither

capability x509/extensions  every extension read as written, unknown ones kept with their criticality, one found by its identifier
  heroes  x509.Extension, x509.Extensions, x509.to_extension, x509.to_extensions, x509.extension_of
  go      x509.Certificate (Extensions, ExtraExtensions, UnhandledCriticalExtensions), pkix.Extension, x509.UnhandledCriticalExtension
  rust    -
  python  x509.Extensions, x509.Extension, x509.ExtensionType, x509.UnrecognizedExtension, x509.Extensions.get_extension_for_oid, x509.Extensions.get_extension_for_class, x509.ExtensionNotFound, x509.DuplicateExtension, x509.ExtensionOID
  note    the twenty-two extensions RFC 5280 defines are decoded into one record, each with whether it was there; the others stand in `unknown`, which `verify_chain` refuses where critical

